In an adorable video the podcaster shared to Instagram on Monday (Dec. 29), she playfully exposes the wholesome fun her country-star husband got up to while she was away. &#8220;Me and the crew flew into Vegas last night, and I woke up this morning to a series of videos from my husband of what&#8217;s going on at the farm while we&#8217;re gone,&#8221; Bunnie began before sharing the clips Jelly sent her.

The camera then cuts to shots &#8212; filmed by Jelly &#8212; of the couple&#8217;s pet cows, Crunch and S&#8217;more, escaping their corrals and running around as helpers try to get them back inside. &#8220;Crunch has gotten out,&#8221; the singer says, cackling. &#8220;Uh oh. This is what happens when you&#8217;re not here, mama.&#8221;

&#8220;When the cat&#8217;s away, the mice will play!&#8221; Jelly hollers. &#8220;Oh, here comes S&#8217;more! Run, S&#8217;more, run!&#8221;

In her caption, Bunnie revealed with a cry-laugh emoji: &#8220;I haven’t even been gone 12 hrs.&#8221;

Jelly and Bunnie first welcomed the cows into their family this past January, along with another bovine named Brownie and a donkey named Griz. “When you went for one mini-cow, but came home with three,&#8221; the Dumb Blonde host wrote on Instagram at the time.

This past year, the couple has also been working to grow their family by welcoming a baby through IVF. Bunnie has been open about the mental and physical toll her fertility treatments have taken on her, venting in an August episode of her podcast how they&#8217;ve kept her from making as may public appearances with her husband.

&#8220;Somebody said the other day, they’re like, ‘They used to always be together. Now you never see them together,&#8217;” she said at the time. “I’m like, do you guys not know for the past six months I’ve been trying to make a baby? &#8230; I literally have been on IVF meds for f—king six months and going through heartbreak and f—king so much s—t.&#8221;

